This package is a port of the `chord` package from pi
(https://github.com/earendil-works/pi), pinned at commit
8eb2bccf2603c28907ef3a583a04cafb1af284ae.

Provenance: this is a fork-and-adapt port, not a clean-room reimplementation.
The upstream sources were read directly and their structure, naming and
algorithms were carried across; the changes are the adaptations to this
repository's runtime and module layout, summarized below and listed per file.

Adaptations, in order of how widely they apply:

  1. Every file: relative specifiers no longer carry a `.ts` suffix, as this
     repository's `check-ts-relative-imports` invariant requires.
  2. Formatting: oxfmt is the only formatter here, so arrow-function bodies are
     parenthesized (`key => ...` becomes `(key) => ...`) and other upstream
     layout differences are normalized.
  3. Entry points: `src/index.ts`, `src/node.ts` and `src/bundler.ts` are
     re-exported through this package's export map, and `src/types.ts` no longer
     separately re-exports `RemoteServiceError`/`RemoteServiceProvider`, which
     the barrel star already carries.
  4. Runtime: `src/context/index.ts` uses `Promise.withResolvers()` instead of a
     hand-rolled Promise constructor; `src/node/bundle.ts` and
     `src/node/package.ts` replace `Awaited<ReturnType<typeof ...>>` with the
     named esbuild `BuildResult` and the `Stats` type from `node:fs`, since this
     repository forbids `ReturnType<>`.
  5. Naming: esbuild externals in `src/node/bundle.ts` match this repository's
     package scope, `@oh-my-pi/chord`, rather than upstream's
     `@earendil-works/chord`.

